>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `harvest_registrations`

``` hol4
Refute.harvest_registrations : unit ->
  {typedefs : hol_type list,
   quotients : hol_type list,
   theories_scanned : string list}
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Eagerly harvests typedef and quotient metadata for the model finder.

The call sweeps every theory in `Theory.ancestry` once, oldest first,
and attempts the standard typedef and quotient harvest for every type
operator those theories declare.  By default the model finder harvests
lazily, the first time a goal mentions an unregistered Abs/Rep
occurrence; this call runs that same harvest ahead of any goal, so every
incompatibility guard, clash guard, and negative-cache entry behaves
identically.

The result lists only what this call newly registered; a type already
registered, explicitly or by an earlier harvest, is omitted, so an
immediate second call returns empty lists.  `theories_scanned` is the
whole swept ancestry, not the narrower set of theories whose theorems
the harvest actually inspected.

### Failure

A type operator that cannot be classified, or that already carries an
incompatible classification, is silently skipped.  Enumerating the
ancestry and each theory's type operators runs outside that handler and
can still raise.

### See also

[`Refute.register_typedef`](#Refute.register_typedef),
[`Refute.register_quotient`](#Refute.register_quotient),
[`Refute.model_refute`](#Refute.model_refute)

Lazy and whole-ancestry harvesting are described in
\ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
